---
// The story: how Sova got here, told impersonally as a log. Public level of
// detail from docs/marketing/comeback-thread.md (old chain, custody, the
// audit, the pivot); dates from the audit of the old chain; the road from
// docs/ROADMAP.md. Site v4: the rebuild beats lead with the vision (contracts
// that see Zcash) and use positive framing. Sources: site/README.md.
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';

// Each beat is a log line: a timestamp (dates only where the record has one)
// and the event, then a few short paragraphs.
const beats = [
  {
    ts: '2025-09', ev: 'v1 on Bitcoin',
    p: [
      'Sova launched in September 2025 as an EVM chain on the OP Stack with native BTC. It ran on mainnet until November 2025.',
    ],
  },
  {
    ts: '2025-11', ev: 'the flaw',
    p: [
      'Native BTC meant someone held the BTC. On Sova v1, a single operator key did, and the chain leaned on outside services to keep running.',
      'A chain that holds other people’s coins is only as strong as whoever holds them. Sova v1 was shut down.',
    ],
  },
  {
    ts: 'audit', ev: 'nothing left behind',
    p: [
      'After shutdown, every derivable custody address was checked. Zero BTC remained.',
    ],
  },
  {
    ts: '2026', ev: 'rebuilt beside Zcash',
    p: [
      'Zcash is private money that works. Money gets useful when programs can react to it.',
      'The usual answer is to wrap ZEC onto another chain, which brings the custody problem straight back. Sova takes the other path: self-custody. The ZEC stays on Zcash, and Sova’s contracts look at it there.',
    ],
  },
  {
    ts: 'design', ev: 'contracts that see Zcash',
    p: [
      'Every Sova node runs its own Zcash node, so a contract can verify a ZEC payment against Zcash itself.',
    ],
  },
  {
    ts: 'design', ev: 'burn to mine',
    p: [
      'Destroy ZEC on Zcash and the next Sova block mints SOVA, the gas, to your EVM address.',
      'One Sova block per Zcash block, ordered by Zcash’s proof-of-work. Every node checks every mint against its own Zcash node.',
    ],
  },
  {
    ts: 'now', ev: 'running',
    p: [
      'One command runs a Zcash node, a Sova node and a miner on a laptop. Nodes find each other over their own protocol, sync, and reject any history with a bad mint.',
    ],
  },
];

const next = [
  'Source, specs and the one-command chain go public.',
  'A public testnet, mined with testnet ZEC, where contracts see Zcash (SIP-4).',
  'Contracts that watch Zcash’s value pools, block by block (SIP-7).',
  'Mainnet when the testnet has earned it.',
];
---
<Site
  title="The Sova story"
  description="Sova started on Bitcoin, where a single key held the BTC. It was shut down, an audit found zero BTC left, and Sova was rebuilt beside Zcash: self-custody, with contracts that see Zcash."
  current="/story"
  cmd="git log --reverse sova"
  status="pre-release · no public network yet"
>
  <h1>The story</h1>
  <p class="lead">Sova started on Bitcoin, learned what custody costs, and was rebuilt beside Zcash: self-custody, with contracts that see Zcash.</p>

  <ol class="beats">
    {beats.map((b) => (
      <li>
        <h2 class="log"><span class="ts">[{b.ts}]</span> <span class="ev">{b.ev}</span></h2>
        {b.p.map((t) => <p>{t}</p>)}
      </li>
    ))}
    <li>
      <h2 class="log"><span class="ts">[next]</span> <span class="ev">the road</span></h2>
      <ul class="bul">
        {next.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="next"><a href="/paper">Read the paper</a><a href="/why">Why Sova</a><a href="/node">Run a node</a></p>
</Site>

<style>
  .beats { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 30px 0 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .beats > li { position: relative; padding: 0 0 26px 22px; max-width: none; }
  .beats > li::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: -4px; top: 0.72em; width: 7px; height: 7px;
    background: var(--g); box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(244, 183, 40, 0.5);
  }
  .beats > li:last-child { padding-bottom: 4px; }
  :global(.page) .beats h2.log { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0; }
  :global(.page) .beats h2.log::before { content: none; }
  .ts { color: var(--g3); font-weight: 400; }
  .ev { color: var(--g); }
  .beats p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; max-width: 64ch; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .beats .bul li { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; max-width: 64ch; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .beats > li { padding-left: 16px; }
    :global(.page) .beats h2.log { font-size: 15.5px; }
    .beats p, .beats .bul li { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; }
  }
</style>
